  4582	   176	## Review Workflow
  4583	   177
  4584	   178	1. Validate every selected acceptance fragment and confirm it was approved by the named authority before its implementation completed. Check current SSOT decision refs and invalidation keys, then dispatch the maximum conflict-free set of ready evidence-review lanes across fragments.
  4585	   179	2. Verify every protected acceptance test still exists and matches its approved hash. Treat deleted tests, weakened assertions, broad skips, unapproved snapshot updates, and fixture-specific production branches as blocking findings.
  4586	   180	3. Reconcile every `AC-*` item in each fragment with fresh or still-valid evidence. Confirm the test layer is strong enough for the claim; screenshots do not prove database side effects, and mocks do not prove a real external integration.
  4587	   181	4. Review implementation quality: module boundaries, reuse, transaction behavior, errors, dependencies, unrelated changes, hidden fallbacks, swallowed failures, hard-coding, and observability.
  4588	   182	5. Review the five machine layers proportionately: static, unit, integration/contract, critical E2E, and applicable non-functional checks.
  4589	   183	6. Verify real sandbox evidence for release-critical external services in addition to mock contracts. Record account/role, environment, timestamp, resource identity, and cleanup state.
  4590	   184	7. Resolve the project-level human workspace from the contract. Verify `binding.md` matches the exact task ID, SSOT path/node, contract version/hash, checklist hash, role, and blocking status. Read its stable checklist and the selected immutable `runs/<run-id>/result.md`; verify the run's contract, binding, and checklist snapshots and hashes before evaluating each signed `H-*` decision. An AI reviewer may prepare or observe the checklist but must not impersonate the product owner for blocking decisions.
  4591	   185	8. Check exploratory findings, rollback readiness, and production monitoring for high-risk changes. Define the metric, threshold, window, owner, and response action; “monitor logs” is not a release control.
  4592	   186	9. Create a new task-local `acceptance/release/runs/<run-id>/` review directory for each reviewed fragment or scoped synthesis. Bind the result to decision refs/invalidation keys, contract version/hash, source identity, runtime identity, and every accepted upstream run ID plus result hash. Never overwrite an earlier review or release decision.
  4593	   187	10. Rebuild and validate all affected task indexes and the project index. In an existing SSOT, reference selected machine, human, and release run IDs and hashes only from the affected nodes. Only each designated acceptance owner may move its node to `ACCEPTED`; only the release-review owner may issue the final release decision.
  4594	   188	11. Write findings first using [`references/release-review-template.md`](references/release-review-template.md). Do not use test counts or code coverage as a completion claim.
